STILL RECORDING, tape 14: "Rule 9" (2026). Halloway Archive. Original story, pictures, sound and music. A work of fiction.

Pictures: drawn in code (canvas 2D) with the tape kit (channel/brand/tapekit.js): a 2.5D renderer, CCTV grading, the handheld camcorder look and VHS damage. The guard office, the night shift rule sheet, the night log, Leon's handwriting (a single-stroke block hand drawn stroke by stroke, no font), his hand on the pen, and the figure over his chair (a soft black silhouette in the style of the kit's 'broken' figure) are drawn for this tape (film.js).
Fonts: VT323 (The VT323 Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1. Special Elite (Astigmatic), Apache License 2.0.
Voice: ElevenLabs text-to-speech, model eleven_v4. Leon Marsh: "HA Leon Marsh" (ElevenLabs Voice Design, made for this series).
Sound effects: generated with ElevenLabs Sound Effects (prompts in sfx/prompts.json).
Music: none. A low drone made from the office's own ventilation (tools/score.py).
Sound: every sound is in the guard office, heard through Leon's camcorder or CAM 02's microphone (tools/mix.py).
